        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "b301c3c0-0685-5cd9-a41e-3b32791a79f5",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Organizations: Cercle Proudhon\n- People: George Valois, Édouard Berth, Georges Sorel, Pierre-Joseph Proudhon\n- Places: France\n- Concepts: mutualism, federalism, property, anarchist philosophy\n- Works: What Is Property?\n- Events: French Revolution of 1848\n\nFacts:\n- Pierre-Joseph Proudhon was a French politician born on 15 January 1809 and died on 19 January 1865.\n- In 1840, Pierre-Joseph Proudhon first published What Is Property?, a nonfiction work about property and its relation to anarchist philosophy.\n- After the French Revolution of 1848, Pierre-Joseph Proudhon became a member of the French Parliament and thereafter described himself as a federalist.\n- Pierre-Joseph Proudhon was the founder of mutualist philosophy.\n- Cercle Proudhon was a political group founded in France on 16 December 1911 by George Valois and Édouard Berth.\n- Cercle Proudhon was inspired by Georges Sorel and by a selective reading of Pierre-Joseph Proudhon.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
